WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:06.070
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.740
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.960
break up foreordination

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.840
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:31.590
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:40.890
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:46.690
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:51.860
Then make ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.120
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.660
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.660
wake up your tough intention
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:02.120
wake up your tough intention

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.040
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:07.290
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:13.930
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.510
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.980
break up foreordination

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.160
Suprise Attack

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.090
Sometime soon...

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:35.810
Suprise Attack

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.390
The ones who killed you;

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.010
we're going to find them.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:42.830
And then...

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:58.380
Um...

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:11.240
Okay, bye!

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.070
Wait.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.070
It was pure chance, really!

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:31.430
I-I just happened to see you in town carrying a bouquet.

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:33.000
So you followed me.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.420
But I didn't mean to listen in.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.960
And I didn't even hear anything!

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.640
So please, carry on.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.950
Bye.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:44.350
It's my sister.

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.140
She died eight years ago.

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:51.400
I didn't ask!

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:56.710
The military says it was a fueling accident at a supply base,

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.900
but I don't believe it.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:06.990
She was made to participate in some kind of secret mission.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.170
How would you know that?

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:14.270
They won't tell me any of the details.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.230
Wouldn't that make you suspicious?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.220
I don't really know.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.070
Sorry to bother you.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.170
That's why I joined the military.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.550
I told you, I didn't ask...

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.020
They say that if you pilot a Trail Krieger,

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.350
you can get promoted quickly for doing good work.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.750
If I can do that, I'll have more chances to find out what the brass is hiding.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.320
With Argevollen...

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:55.090
About that... are you serious?

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.270
Yeah.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:03:58.840
I'm serious.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.010
Are you retarded?

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:05.820
You have your hands full just getting Argevollen to move,

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:09.450
and you're talking success, promotions, and military secrets?

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:10.570
You're shitting me!

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:11.630
There's no way!

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:12.810
Are you dreaming?

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.810
You don't have to put it like that!

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.590
Has it ever occurred to you that you might die?

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.130
It's all good so long as I don't, right?

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:44.840
I want to change pilots!

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:49.060
Private Susumu is still green, as both a pilot and a soldier.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:52.120
And that makes him naïve...

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:54.980
Or reckless? No, that's not it.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.000
I know! He's inexperienced!

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.640
To be blunt, I fear for his life!

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:12.380
If that happens, the machine might be destroyed.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:16.280
That means the project will be terminated.

00:05:16.890 --> 00:05:19.550
Not only will we be unable to gather data...

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:24.290
Well...

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:27.220
Recording complete.

00:05:27.870 --> 00:05:29.570
Will you leave this message?

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:48.610
You're a total newbie, too!

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.830
Ow...

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.580
Our scouts report that the area

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.110
between the Great Wall and the Gate of No Retreat

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:02.420
is already under enemy control.

00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:07.830
The enemy has divided its forces there and joined with its rear units.

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:12.600
They'll be attacking the capital, Ajuas, from at least three directions.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.600
Those bastards just won't give up.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.520
Here, in the Arida mountain range, is where the enemy is advancing most rapidly.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.260
We've managed to hold them back with the 3rd Knight Battalion so far,

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:25.980
but we can't afford to be lax.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:29.180
Colonel, that's enough of an introduction.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:29.910
Yes, sir!

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:35.830
And so, Lieutenant, we'd like you to mobilize Independent Unit 8.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.260
That new model!

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:39.830
Use that.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:43.600
If you can win even more glory here,

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:46.720
you might be worthy of a provisional Royal Memorial Medal!

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:48.290
I'll endeavor to do so.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:51.090
We're counting on you.

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:51.840
Yes, sir!

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.090
Samonji.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.200
I'm sorry.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.590
I couldn't even give you a real break.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:05.220
It's fine.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:07.990
There's no resting here, anyway.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:10.950
Good luck.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:22.420
What do you think about that Samonji guy?

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:26.370
There's honestly not much interesting about him.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:30.840
He didn't bat an eyelid at the mention of a Royal Memorial Medal.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:35.350
He might be the type who wants to stay on the battlefield his whole life.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.350
What about that Trail Krieger?

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:42.670
Just as Junios's speech said, it's a fantasy.

00:07:42.670 --> 00:07:47.070
In a real war like the one we've got now, it's of no use whatsoever.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.170
We'll be leaving at 1500.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:53.560
We'll head through the mountains and arrive in Arida at 2400,

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.370
where we'll rendezvous with the 3rd Knights.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:59.450
From there on, we'll be under their command.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:03.000
There's not much time before the mission begins.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.010
Make sure you get plenty of sleep while we're on the move,

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:09.600
and memorize the entire geography of the area around Arida.

00:08:11.930 --> 00:08:12.670
Dismissed.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:19.250
The master sergeant wants the impossible.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.410
What's his problem?

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:39.270
Tokimune's got a chip on his shoulder!

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:40.200
What's up?

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.530
Did something happen?

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:43.880
No, it's nothing. Let's go.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.990
Thank you for traveling so far to join us, Brigadier General Zarl.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:14.000
It was easier getting here than I thought. We didn't see the enemy at all.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:19.300
That's all thanks to your efforts, Lt. Colonel Holmes.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.830
Thank you.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:25.340
His Excellency Junios must be quite pleased, as well.

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:27.830
Keep up the good work.

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:29.970
You honor me.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:33.190
I'll do everything I can.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:38.340
By the way, where is the pilot who fought the enemy's new model?

00:09:56.850 --> 00:09:57.870
Who are you?

00:09:57.870 --> 00:09:59.660
Brigadier General Zarl wants to speak to you.

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.020
Back to the front lines, huh?

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:14.330
Stop grumbling and get in.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:20.750
I can't die here.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:30.900
Excuse me.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:33.210
Over here.

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:34.010
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:41.870
Just now, I got word from your boss.

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:45.200
From Mr. Sugoro?

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:50.210
The answer to the message you almost left on his answering machine is "no."

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:51.930
Well, yes..

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:56.670
What, was he pretending to not be there and listening on the other side of the phone?

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.160
As for us,

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:03.180
We have no intention of removing Private Susumu from his position as pilot, either.

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:10.770
You're putting a lot of faith in him, don't you think?

00:11:16.540 --> 00:11:19.770
Without him, you wouldn't be here.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:22.520
We're departing.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:23.090
Yes, sir.

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:43.760
So, what was your impression?

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:50.550
How did the enemy's new model compare to Ingelmia's latest Trail Kriegers?

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:52.390
There's no way to compare them.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:53.760
What do you mean?

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.250
It was decisive.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.470
The new enemy unit is

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:01.850
a fundamental departure from our concept of what a Trail Krieger is.

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:03.530
Its capabilities are unknown.

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:08.100
That's quite a thing to say with that expressionless face.

00:12:08.590 --> 00:12:09.870
You asked me.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.410
Very well.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:13.940
Anything else?

00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:14.890
Nothing.

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:18.550
Then you may leave.

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:34.060
Is Lt. Colonel Holmes there? Put him on.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.170
It's me.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:42.010
I've decided we need to acquire the enemy's new model, by any means necessary.

00:12:42.760 --> 00:12:45.590
I'll handle the flies in intelligence.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:51.030
I'm a former Krieger pilot myself, you know.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.370
I want to see this exceptional machine for myself, you know?

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:13.290
Independent Unit 8 has arrived.

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:16.290
Welcome. I'm Iriki.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.860
From the right, they are Yaida, Tanizaki, and Nishijima.

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:23.570
I'd like to discuss the operation right away.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.370
The target is the enemy front-line base.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:32.450
The battalion will attack from three separate routes, and we will attack from the northwest.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:35.000
The problem is this plain.

00:13:35.520 --> 00:13:37.120
The terrain has some small changes in elevation,

00:13:37.120 --> 00:13:38.830
but beyond that, there is no cover.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:44.080
We'll need to traverse 800 meters in order to reach the forest where the enemy base is located.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:48.170
The top speed of a Kokuyou is 55 km/h.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:52.560
Even if we run straight through at top speed, it'll take more than a minute.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:53.350
Well shit.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:58.530
And I'm sure the enemy will be waiting for us en masse.

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:00.580
We'll be riddled with bullets.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.070
That's why we'll be using these flares.

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:04.510
That's right.

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:09.790
Once the operation begins, each unit will fire a flare to reveal itself,

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.360
forcing the enemy to divide its targets.

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:13.580
What does the enemy have?

00:14:14.180 --> 00:14:18.630
At a minimum, three 203mm long-range guns in the enemy base.

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.590
Those things are frighteningly accurate.

00:14:21.990 --> 00:14:24.160
They take about a minute to load.

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:26.840
Their observers are probably skilled, with good night vision.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:30.340
Inside the forest, they won't be able to target us,

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:33.850
but it'll be tough to deal with them when we're crossing the plain.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:37.470
Therefore, Argevollen will be leading the offensive.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:42.970
Use your speed to draw the enemy's attention and break through their front line.

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:44.860
Can you do that?

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:47.110
Yes, sir.

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.250
Leave the cover fire to us.

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:49.830
Right!

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:51.620
Any other questions?

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.000
The operation will begin at 0300.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:58.990
The seeker will go on ahead and provide backup.

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:01.630
We'll hold muster for everyone else in 40 minutes.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.250
Now, let's get started.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:18.440
Jamie, get something to eat while you can.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:19.750
Oh, yeah.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:21.600
But can I wait a little longer?

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.610
You can let Tokimune do that!

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.070
No, this is my job.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:31.760
Jamie...

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.310
Can I talk to you?

00:15:38.770 --> 00:15:39.620
What is it?

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:44.000
About Jamie...

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.090
Is she complaining again?

00:15:46.480 --> 00:15:48.520
She's working hard.

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:50.550
Huh?

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.800
I'm sorry. She isn't descriptive enough.

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:59.690
We just saw Jamie tuning Argevollen without even taking the time to eat.

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.690
Jamie, of all people...

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:04.100
I don't know what happened,

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:06.720
but you need to understand how Jamie feels.

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:11.280
How Jamie feels?

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:42.720
Okay.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.060
Is it ready?

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:54.490
Yeah.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.960
Manipulation. Tokimune Susumu, active.

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.360
Protocol recognized.

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:16.220
Power converters 1, 2, and 3 have reached criticality.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:18.730
Weapon expansion online.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:21.150
Argevollen, all systems go.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:24.860
Looks like everything is nominal.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:42.500
Maybe it's best that it was you.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:46.920
Somebody who thought they might die

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.630
might not have been able to operate this Krieger.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:06.730
I'll do what I need to do!

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:14.540
So let's both do our best.

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:33.200
I want to make sure of this, just so there's no mistake.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.380
Okay, stop! Stop!

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:44.350
Jamie, are you...

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:51.190
in love with me?

00:19:19.900 --> 00:19:20.910
No.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.820
Tokimune...

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:56.470
Yes?

00:19:57.700 --> 00:20:01.510
I think I just kinda fell in love with you.

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.510
I see. Thank you!

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:12.490
That idiot is too direct...

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:15.560
Yeah, you wouldn't normally say that on the move, huh?

00:20:41.620 --> 00:20:42.960
Ready the flares.

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:50.640
Once the flares go up, don't move until I give the signal.

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:28.930
Seeker, how many flares do you see?

00:21:29.740 --> 00:21:32.120
Just the one we fired.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:33.180
Anyway, Captain,

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:35.650
the enemy is on the move.

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:36.990
What's going on?

00:21:36.990 --> 00:21:40.950
It seems there was trouble with the three flares

00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:42.610
the battalion was going to fire!

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:43.340
What?

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:40.060
Run, Jamie!
